<title>GERMANY: TABLE-German May trade surplus falls to 9.8 bln DM.</title>
<headline>TABLE-German May trade surplus falls to 9.8 bln DM.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal</p>
<p>Statistics Office reported the following preliminatry economic</p>
<p>data (bln marks): GERMAN TRADE/CURRENT ACC  May 97  April 97</p>
<p>May 96</p>
<p> Trade balance		 +9.8    +10.4	    +9.2</p>
<p> Current account	     -2.5     +3.2	    -2.9</p>
<p> Exports			 70.8     73.3	    64.5</p>
<p> Imports			 61.0     62.9	    55.3</p>
<p> Services			-4.9     -2.9	    -4.8</p>
<p> Wage and property income  -3.2     +0.3	    -2.1</p>
<p> Transfers		     -3.8     -4.5	    -5.1</p>
<p> Supplementary trade	 -0.4     -0.1	    -0.1 GERMAN</p>
<p>TRADE/CURRENT ACC Jan-May 97	Jan-May 96</p>
<p> Trade balance		  +44.6	     +36.0</p>
<p> Current account		 -7.8		-5.7</p>
<p> Exports			  346.8	     319.1</p>
<p> Imports			  302.2	     283.1</p>
<p> Services			 -21.2	     -19.7</p>
<p> Wage and property income    -8.2		+0.6</p>
<p> Transfers			-21.9	     -21.8</p>
<p> Supplementary trade	   -1.1		-0.8</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
